From ab898edd991fb6d46496b05524ba96e2496166cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zimbermanne <zimbermanne@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 06:36:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Replace frosted glass with liquid glass (SVG refraction +
 chromatic aberration)

- Add LiquidGlassFilter.jsx: SVG feDisplacementMap-based filter with
  3-channel chromatic aberration split + feSpecularLighting highlight,
  mounted once at the true app root (needs to sit above the router
  since public routes render outside the authenticated Layout/app-shell)
- design-tokens.css: --glass-blur/--glass-blur-sm now start as plain
  blur() (universal fallback), upgraded to the liquid filter via
  @supports (backdrop-filter: url(...)) feature detection -- no browser
  sniffing, degrades cleanly on Firefox/older Safari
- Convert every remaining hardcoded backdrop-filter: blur(...) in
  globals.css (light mode + both dark-mode override blocks) and
  Landing.jsx's inline styles onto the token system, so the whole app
  upgrades consistently instead of a partial frost/liquid mix
  - full filter: .card, .modal, .sidebar, .glass-panel, .lg-glass(-card)
  - -sm (lighter, no chromatic split) for high-frequency small elements:
    inputs, badges, table headers, buttons, dropdown menu, landing pills
- Add contain: layout paint style (+ will-change on sticky elements) to
  .card, .sidebar, .mobile-topbar to isolate paint cost -- matters most
  for sidebar/topbar since they repaint on every scroll frame
